Title: SwitchIfEmpty on a Subject
Description: I have an issue with the Observable.switchIfEmpty operator. It’s not called properly. See sample code

```kotlin
class TestObs {

    @Test
    fun testSwitchIfEmpty() {
        val subject = BehaviorSubject.create<List<String>>()
        subject.onNext(listOf("a"))
        subject.test().assertValueCount(1)

        // works
//        Observable.create<List<String>> { emitter ->
//            emitter.onNext(listOf("a"))
//            emitter.onComplete()
//        }

        // fails
        subject
            .flatMapIterable { it }
            .filter { it == "c" }
            .switchIfEmpty(Observable.create { emitter ->
                emitter.onNext("c")
                emitter.onComplete()
            })
            .test()
            .assertValue("c")
    }
}
```

I just want to filter "c" and if there is no "c" switch to a new Observable an emit a "c". 

This works if the origin of my rx chain starts with an Observable, but my test fails if my source is a subject. Does this make any sense to you?

Thanks!

